12102150899727396,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":84.9,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.03655795402294748,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":54.6,"_gate_rev_durability":0.013377369781600867,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":31.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.061360401335360144,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":79.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.056597163060767564,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00778,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"BGC Group, Inc. operates as a financial brokerage and technology company in the United States, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. The company offers various brokerage services, such as government bonds and corporate bonds as well as interest rate derivatives and credit derivatives, foreign exchange, fixed income products, equities and futures and options; and brokerage and trade execution of ECS products, including listed derivatives and physical commodities in the oil and refined, and environmental and energy transition markets; and ship chartering services. It also provides price discovery, trade execution, brokerage services, clearing, information, and other back-office services to financial and non-financial institutions. The company also operates BGC Compute Infrastructure Markets, a division focused on the secondary market for compute and memory capacity. In addition, the company offers financial technology solutions, network and connectivity solutions, market data and related information services, market infrastructure, and post-trade services. Further, the company's integrated platform is designed to provide flexibility to customers regarding price discovery, trade execution and processing of transactions, as well as accessing liquidity through its platforms, for transactions executed either OTC or through an exchange. It primarily serves banks, broker-dealers, trading firms, hedge funds, governments, corporations, investment firms, commodity trading firms, and end users. BGC Group, Inc. was founded in 1945 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Sean A. Windeatt | COO & Co-CEO | Age 52 | Compensation: $8.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $649K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 5%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $82K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 12\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["BGC Group, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $5.2B market cap on $2.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 8% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $373M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.54\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 3.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 18% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 45% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","17 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"BGC Group (BGC) Just Gave Investors Something To Think About","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-bgc/bgc-group/news/bgc-group-bgc-just-gave-investors-something-to-think-about","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794561495.338,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"IBKR vs. BGC: Which Tech-Driven Brokerage Stock Is the Better Bet?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3027465/ibkr-vs-bgc-which-tech-driven-brokerage-stock-is-the-better-bet?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cmost_popular_stocks-3027465","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794337080.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Technical Reactions to BGC Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/Technical_Reactions_to_BGC_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_111026025602_1794297362.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794297362.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"BGC or HOOD: Which Is the Better Value Stock Right Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3026601/bgc-or-hood-which-is-the-better-value-stock-right-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_3-3026601","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794238802.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[